Create private, high-throughput connections between Azure datacenters and your existing on-premises or hybrid infrastructure. ExpressRoute connections don’t use the public Internet, so they offer more reliability, faster speeds, lower latencies, and higher security than regular connections. We have a 99.9% SLA in place for connection uptime, and two new bandwidth tiers for Exchange Providers: 200 Mbps and 500 Mbps in addition to 1 Gbps and 10 Gbps tiers. ExpressRoute service will be available in Silicon Valley, Washington DC and London through AT&amp;T NetBond, Equinix, Level3 Communications, British Telecom and Verizon.  We are also pleased to announce strategic partnerships with TeleCity Group and SingTel for Europe and APAC markets. <a href="https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/services/expressroute/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Learn more about ExpressRoute</a>.

If you were already using the preview version of ExpressRoute, you can keep using it at preview pricing rates until July 1st, 2014. Or, choose a lower connection speed and pay the General Availability rate. The <a href="https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/pricing/details/expressroute/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ExpressRoute Pricing details page </a>has a comprehensive look at pricing. If you want to disable ExpressRoute for your account, sign into the <a href="https://manage.windowsazure.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Azure Management Portal</a>.

